  "body": "## Result\n\nA two-call dirty-connector construction where the source changes by `x' = x + C u` and the second call's map changes from `B1` to `B2 = B1 + R`. The uniquely required connector patch is\n\n```text\n(B1 + B2) x' + B1 C u.\n```\n\nFor the uniform family `B1 = J_n`, `C = e0 + e1`, `R = E00`, `n >= 2`, the source change is invisible to `B1`, and the rank-one patch `R x'` moves the open connector directly to the `B2 x'` boundary. The same construction extends to any nonzero even-weight `C` and unit `R=E_(i,j)` with `C_j=1`. The complete input/output map and proof are in `research/rank-one-connector-delta-seed0e9d/PROOF.md`.\n\n## Fully charged local cost\n\nThe exact parity circuit uses one clean scalar scratch bit `t`, supplied and released at the pair boundary for a common complete cost `p_t`. The comparator is stronger than two independent calls: it carries the same parity bit across the pair but restores the connector between outputs.\n\n```text\nconnector-restored baseline: 10n + 4 + p_t\nrank-one transition pair:      8n + 4 + p_t\nsaving:                              2n\n```\n\nAt `n=4`, this is `44+p_t` versus `36+p_t`, saving eight scalar ADDs. Strict independent calls cost `52+p_t`. The package also gives a no-scratch direct row-add schedule (`80 -> 50` at `n=4`) and clearly labels it as a reference count, not a minimum linear-circuit bill. In the complete-call notation, improvement requires `c_B1 + c_B2 > c_patch + Delta_I`; all additional supplier, routing, dispatch, copy, frame, hosting and precision charges belong in those terms.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The general connector transition identity checked on all **32,768** 2x2 map/source/dirty-input choices, plus **444,800** small even-`C`/unit-`R` transition states.\n- The concrete map and inverse checked on all **2,236,928** `x,u,z,y1,y2` inputs per schedule for `n=2..5`, with the factored schedule's declared `t=0` scratch.\n- Literal factored gate lists and reverse programs checked on **180** basis columns across `n=2..5`.\n- Four controls reject omitted rank-one patch, stale source in the patch, closing with `B1` instead of `B2`, and dropping `B1 C u` when `B1 C != 0`.\n- `make selected-record-check` passes. The selected conditional record remains unchanged; its full `make frontier1094-verify` replay was not run because this package does not alter that construction.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/rank-one-connector-delta-seed0e9d/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/rank-one-connector-delta-seed0e9d --check-only\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/rank-one-connector-delta-seed0e9d\n```\n\nThe local host has Python 3.14.7 but no Python 3.12. The direct verifier and metadata check pass locally; the registered Python 3.12 replay is expected from PR CI.\n\n## Scope, sources, overlap\n\nTrack `recursive-interfaces`, task `persistent-boundary` refined to a rank-one map delta after an additive source update. Accepted OS seed: `0e9d3469c47e870c84c141c97ae63540`; priority revision 3; exact base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\n`SOURCES.json` pins the selected record, current review, selected source manifest, assembly certificate, reproduction rule/verifier, catalogue, and nearest prior connector packages. Nearby results are credited: Ross Richardson/PR934; Woklerx's same-map `B C u` adapter and fixed-map delivery-cut optimum (commit `7c573bc769798ce4e336fd5be630060bd9d69a71`); Navinor/PR1155; Hanson Sun/PR1522 and PR1524; and PR1707's common-A broadcast. This work changes the source/map contract; it does not repeat read-free restoration, a fixed-map source tour, or output fanout.\n\nThe latest overlap helper at 2026-10-14 08:17:13 UTC covered 418 open PRs and 371 Discussion/comment/reply records with complete pagination, no warnings, and zero direct matches for the scope query. A supplemental REST read returned 126 current Discussion records. The exact adjacent work and limitations are recorded in `CLAIM.md`; this is not a novelty certificate.\n\nThis is a bounded local construction, not a selected-supplier admission or new `kappa`. No hosted caller, recursive tariff, tape realization, all-size assembly or precision transfer is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\nCinna Davis, with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, exact checks, cost accounting and prose; Apache-2.0.\n",
